A supercell of Fe3GeTe2 monolayer with the size of 60 nm × 60 nm
is used in our simulation. In this supercell, nonmagnetic Ge and Te atoms are ignored, only Fe honeycomb lattice is kept. A round ferromagnetic domain is initially set in the center of the supercell, where the
magnetic moments are pointing along +z/-z directions inside/outside
the domain wall. The magnetic configuration of the system is then relaxed to the equilibrium state. The round domain can gradually relax to
a stable skyrmion or shrink and eventually disappear in the background
depending on the magnetic parameters used in the simulation.
